From 2ef3764707afec127d71cdb23a17d5d79e3738dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:18:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mcp): warn at add_tool when the tool's speed is outside
 the machine's range

A catalog tool above the mounted machine's spindle_max (EM-0300-2FL,
15000 rpm, on the 10000 rpm Tormach 770MX) entered the document with no
word. The first word was the machine check at verify, after the work was
generated, and that line did not name a fix.

- AddTool::with_holder reads the mounted machine and carries a warning
  when the posted speed is above spindle_max or below spindle_min.
- MCP add_tool returns it as "warning"; the UI's add shows it in the
  status line. The tool keeps its stated speed.
- The machine check's problem line for an operation, and the default
  machine's, end with the same fix: set the tool's speed (edit_tool) or
  apply_cutting_data. An NC-line finding keeps its old text.

The check, the post gate and posted G-code do not change.

Fixes #3792

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
